    "pressure": {
      "file": "gear_assembly_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Pitch circles roll; force acts along the line of action",
      "description": "Mating gears behave like pitch circles rolling without slipping: speed ratio = z_driven / z_driver (here 48/16 = 3; the idler changes direction only). Tooth force acts along the line of action at the pressure angle (20°), splitting into a tangential (torque) and a separating (radial) component that the bearings carry. Correct centre distance gives the designed backlash; contact pattern, lubrication and alignment decide gear life (pitting, scuffing, tooth breakage).",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
